  "Question": "A parabola \\(y=ax^2+bx+c\\) has vertex \\((4,2).\\) If \\((2,0)\\) is on the parabola, then \\(abc\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-12\\)",
    "B": "\\(-6\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The vertex \\((4,2)\\) lets us write the parabola in vertex form with only its scale factor unknown:\n\\[\ny=a(x-4)^2+2,\n\\qquad a\\ne0.\n\\]\nSince \\((2,0)\\) lies on the parabola,\n\\[\n0=a(2-4)^2+2=4a+2,\n\\]\nso \\(a=-\\tfrac12\\). Expanding identifies the coefficients in the requested general form:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-\\frac12(x^2-8x+16)+2\\\\\n&=-\\frac12x^2+4x-6.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus \\(a=-\\tfrac12\\), \\(b=4\\), and \\(c=-6\\), giving\n\\[\nabc=\\left(-\\frac12\\right)(4)(-6)=12.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
